      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a95256f54d514123c1f089d|full_name}: Actually, I disagree with that...I would agree that at the current state, smartphones won't be able to properly run VRChat.\n\nThere's plenty of VR Apps made for (yes although they're specifically for, they're on the platform regardless) Android and iOS. They run fine and are a pretty decent experience for VR...let's be honest, if you're relying on a smartphone for an in-depth VR experience, you're in a niche' market and not the target audience for the majority of VR...However, I'd like to see VRChat further progress into the smartphone market also.\nVRChat does what they can to support every VR device...so why not mobile VR?\n\nAtop that,\n\"Smartphones can't handle a VR game, at all.\"\nAre you using a phone from 2004? My phone can run every game I throw at it fine, and it's quite dated as it is (LG G4 (2005 release)).\nFurthermore, with that attitude, nothing will ever progress to smartphones, whereas we should be welcoming it. It won't be perfect off the bat, and you'd be an idiot to think it would be...but the VRChat devs are mere indie developers...they will take their time getting there, and when they are 'there', the experience will be just as nice as the desktop version (cough).\n\nBut honestly...your comment is a little biased.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
